  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Everyone against everyone – feint and dribble past",
  "description": "Everyone has a puck and moves freely inside a box of about 10 × 10 metres. When you meet a team-mate you take them on, make a feint and dribble past – but nobody may take or knock the puck away from anyone else. Then you carry on with your own puck and look for the next one to take on.\n\nProgression: skate with the puck with only one hand on the stick. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Where are your stick and puck best placed when you take someone on?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Why might it help to feint before you dribble?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Change pace after the feint – get past with speed."
    }
  ],
